        "original_id": "13d589d0-2d47-52ec-bbbe-8819ba8b6d9f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Kansas, Kansas City area\n- Systems: K-10, I-70\n- Products: The Day After\n- Organizations: ABC television network, De Soto High School\n\nFacts:\n- In 1982, several scenes for the TV film The Day After were filmed on K-10 in Kansas to portray a mass exodus from the Kansas City area on I-70.\n- On November 20, 1983, The Day After first aired on the ABC television network.\n- During its initial broadcast, The Day After earned a 46 rating and a 62% audience share.\n- Up to that time, The Day After was the seventh highest-rated non-sports television show and the highest-rated television film in history.\n- As of a 2009 report, The Day After still held the record for the highest-rated television film in history.\n- K-10 is a 38-mile (61 km) state highway in Kansas.\n- De Soto High School is located off K-10 and Lexington Avenue on 91st Street in Kansas.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
